Compute outside-bark stem volume from a segment table

\code{compute_stem_volume} aggregates the per-slice cylinder or circle fits
returned by \code{\link[=stem_segments]{stem_segments()}} or \code{\link[=segment_stem]{segment_stem()}} into
per-tree outside-bark stem volume estimates.  Two volume formulae are
available: the simple cylinder formula and Smalian's formula for tapering
stems.

The only required columns are \code{TreeID}, \code{Segment}, \code{Z_low}, \code{Z_high},
\code{Radius}, and \code{Valid}.  All other columns (\code{RANSAC_err}, \code{N_inliers}, etc.)
are used when present but are not required.

A \code{data.frame} with one row per tree and columns:
